# Lesson 2, from exercise 2c: partner opens 1♣, you respond with a flat 8. Student sits South.
title: A flat hand: 1NT over 1♣
id: L02-26
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3
student: S
board: 36
dealer: W
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AQ4    K82    J5     KJT63
  E  JT82   A543   A764   2
  S  763    QJ9    K982   Q54
  W  K95    T76    QT3    A987

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1C     = 13+ points, at least four clubs
  E Pass
  S 1NT*   = 6-9 points, balanced
     key: 8 HCP and a flat hand. The rule list points to 2♣ with three clubs, but in practice 1NT describes this hand best.
     not 2C: The rules point to 2♣, but did you notice how flat your hand is? 1NT says so in one bid.
     not 1D: 1♦ is allowed, but with such a flat hand, doesn't 1NT tell partner more?
     not Pass: Did you count 8? With 6 or more, keep the auction open.
     not *: With 6-9 and a flat hand, which response describes it in one bid?
  W Pass
  N Pass   = No game: partner has a minimum
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner opened 1♣. The rule list points to a raise to 2♣ with three
  clubs, but with a flat 8 points, 1NT describes your hand best. Partner
  passed, so there is no game. You are declarer, because you bid no-trump
  first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W HT  N H2  E HA  S H9
  2   E H3  S HJ  W H6  N H8
      note: East returns partner's suit.
  3   S CQ  W C7  N C3  E C2
      note: The plan: set up dummy's clubs. Play the queen first, the high card from your short side.
  4   S C4  W C8  N CK  E S2
      note: Keep leading clubs until the ace is gone.
  5   N CJ  E D4  S C5  W CA
      note: Keep going. West takes the ace.
  6   W H7  N HK  E H5  S HQ
  7   N CT  E S8  S S3  W C9
      note: Dummy's clubs are winners now.
  8   N C6  E D6  S S6  W S5
      note: The last club.
  9   N SA  E ST  S S7  W S9
      note: Cash the ♠A.
  10  N DJ  E D7  S D2  W DQ
      note: Seven tricks are in. Lead a diamond and let the defense take the rest.
  11  W DT  N D5  E DA  S D8
  12  E H4  S D9  W D3  N S4
  13  E SJ  S DK  W SK  N SQ
      note: 7 tricks: 1NT made.

play recap:
  The plan: set up dummy's clubs, keeping the ♠A and ♥K as ways to reach
  them.

  1NT made. Your 1NT told partner about your strength and your flat shape
  in a single bid.
